# "Pocket AI" Is a Fixed Brand Name

The AI assistant feature in this app is called **Pocket AI**. This name is final.

## Rule

**Never change, rename, shorten, translate, or rebrand "Pocket AI" without explicit permission from the project owner.**

Do not do any of the following on your own initiative:

- Rename it to "AI Copilot", "Copilot", "AI", "Pocket Assistant", "Gemini", "Assistant", or anything else.
- Translate the label ("पॉकेट AI", "Pocket एआई", etc.) or create per-language brand variants.
- Abbreviate it to "PAI", "P.AI", "PocketAI" (no space), or similar.
- Change its casing ("Pocket Ai", "pocket ai", "POCKET AI").
- Change the brand in only one place and leave others inconsistent.
- Use a different name in user-facing copy, tooltips, button labels, settings titles, hints, toasts, error messages, or docs.
- Rename related identifiers, files, or components as if the rename were requested. Internal code names (`copilot`, `AiCopilotLayout`, `data-pl-ocr-ai-copilot-toggle`, etc.) are implementation detail — leave them alone unless asked.

## User-facing label

Wherever the user sees the feature name, it must read exactly:

```
Pocket AI
```

Examples:

```tsx
// ❌ BAD
<Section title="AI Copilot" />
<Button>AI Copilot</Button>
title={on ? "Hide AI Copilot" : "Open AI Copilot beside the form"}

// ✅ GOOD
<Section title="Pocket AI" />
<Button>Pocket AI</Button>
title={on ? "Hide Pocket AI" : "Open Pocket AI beside the form"}
```

## Companion rule

"AI Copilot" is the retired name. If you encounter it in new code or new copy, that is a bug — use "Pocket AI".

## Allowed exceptions

- User-visible names of *other* products or services (e.g. "Gemini" as the underlying model, "Google Drive") stay as they are.
- Internal identifiers, CSS hooks, storage keys, and type names may keep their existing names; renaming them is a refactor, not this rule.

## If a rename is genuinely needed

Stop and ask the project owner first. Do not proceed on an inferred or partial instruction.
